      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/charlottsville_pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A stretch of the Pittsburgh Line of the Norfolk Southern Railway forms Charlottsville’s northwestern boundary, linking it to Altoona and Pittsburgh.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlottsville%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In the 1850s Scotch‑Irish and German pioneers cleared the Little Juniata valley for farms and mills, shaping the area’s early economy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/charlottsville_pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Housing in Charlottsville is almost evenly split between owner‑occupied and renter‑occupied units, most three‑bedroom homes valued between $100,000 and $149,999.",
